  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "This pan heats on an induction cooktop without a directly heated burner. The cooktop sends energy into the pan using a changing magnetic field. Below the glass, high frequency alternating current flows through a copper coil. That field drives circular electric currents inside the magnetic metal pan. Electrical resistance turns their energy into heat so the pan itself gets hot. The pan then conducts that heat into the food. A suitable magnetic pan is essential. Ordinary glass or copper alone will not work. So the coil creates the field but the resistant pan becomes the heater.",
